Hi,

Here is the first proposal to add device class major/minor class
setup. It is not following the BlueZ API document yet. I am
considering the class one property (GetProperty / SetProperty).


Some issues to be discussed:
1. Is it needed sent a signal to notify the major/minor class changes?
2. Should we use string to represent the major/minor classes?
Define strings to represent the minor class can be painful :)

3. Should the minor class be a writeable property for all device classes?
eg: Access Point uses the minor class to represent the load. IMHO,
maybe we need check if the D-Bus clients can overwrite the minor
class. Is there another minor class with the same problem?


How test:
$dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --dest=3Dorg.bluez --print-reply
/org/bluez/Device/hci0 org.bluez.Device.SetProperty string:"class"
byte:1 byte:3

$dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --dest=3Dorg.bluez --print-reply
/org/bluez/Device/hci0 org.bluez.Device.GetProperty string:"class"


Regards,
Claudio.
--
---------------------------------------------------------
Claudio Takahasi
Instituto Nokia de Tecnologia - INdT

